a-bi a-ta bé-li a-ta a-dí lu-qú-ut-kà ša Tí-me-el-ki-a a-na Wa-ah-šu-ša-na ú-ša-lá-ma-ni-ma ITI.1.KAM iš-tí-in ú ší-na ITI.2.KAM a-sà-hu-ru i-na lu-qú-tí-kà ṣú-ba-tí 10 SIG5 ú 20 ší-ma-am ma-ah-ra-am ša lu-bu-ší-šu a-kà-lá-ma a-ší-am 15 GÍN za-ku-am ša ša-ru-tim ša-ma-am-ma A-lu-wa iš-tí ba-tí-qí-im ṭù-ur-da-ma.,"My dear father and lord: until your goods from Timelkiya arrive safely in Wahšušana and I shall wait one or two months, I shall hold some 10 or 20 fine textiles from your shipment for the first sale for his clothes, and then buy for me some 15 shekels of ašium, pure and of royal quality, and send Aluwa with a bātiqum …","Barjamovic, Gojko - A Historical Geography of Ancient Anatolia in the Assyrian Colony Period. CNI 38, 2011.pdf",185
