i-Ha-qá uš-ba-ku,I am currently residing in Haqa.,"Barjamovic, Gojko - A Historical Geography of Ancient Anatolia in the Assyrian Colony Period. CNI 38, 2011.pdf",128
i-na e-ri-qí-im a-Pu-ru-uš-ha-tim A-lá-hu-um ù Wa-li-a ub-lu-šum.,Ali-ahum and Waliya brought … to him to Purušhattum in a wagon.,"Barjamovic, Gojko - A Historical Geography of Ancient Anatolia in the Assyrian Colony Period. CNI 38, 2011.pdf",64
ú a-na-ku a-dí mu-ṣí-im pá-al-ha-ku-ma a-na qá-qí-dí-a ù na-pá-áš-tí lu-qú-tí-kà a-na Pu-ru-uš-ha-dim e-ra-ba-am ú-lá a-mu-a a-dí a-ší-im ša pá-kà a-na mu-ṣí-im ta-dí-nu-ma a-ší-am lá tù-šé-bi4-[l]a-ni-ma li-bi a-we-LAM lá tù-na-e-hu a-ta la tí-de8-e ki-ma a-we-LAM a-ba-am lá-am-nu-ma a-na a-bi-šu kà-ša-dí-im i-lu-ku.,"And as for me, I was afraid because of the mūṣium and because of fear for my own head and the welfare of your goods I will not enter Purušhaddum. With regard to the ašium-metal that you promised to the mūṣium without sending any ašium and thereby not calming the man’s heart – do you not know that the man is hostile towards the father and will go to reach his father?","Barjamovic, Gojko - A Historical Geography of Ancient Anatolia in the Assyrian Colony Period. CNI 38, 2011.pdf",392
a-na Ú-ṣur-ša-A-šur qí-bi-ma um-ma DINGIR-i-dí-ma a-ma-la tù-ša-hi-zi-ni a-na É.GAL.lim e-li-ma té-i-ra-tí-kà a-tù-ú-ma um-ma ru-ba-um-ma ma-la ú-na-hi-du-šu-ni a-wa-tí-a ú-kà-al um-ma ru-ba-um-ma a-šu-mì KÙ.GI ú ša Šu-lu-a-at té-er-tám ub-la-ni a-na Wa-ah-šu-<ša>-na a-ša-pá-ar ú pé-er-dam ú-šé-ba-al a-pu-tum a-na Wa-ah-šu-ša-na šé-ep-kà la ta-ša-kà-an a-dí ru-ba-am Pu-ru-uš-ha-tí-am ú Ú-šu-na-la-am ú Wa-ah-šu-ša-na-i-am ra-bi sí-ki-tim ú-ta-mu-ú ú-la i-la-kam a-na-kam i-ma-at Ša-ar-la Ša-bu-a-i-ú ha-ra-na-am ú-kà-i-lu-ni-a-tí-ma i-ṣa-áb-tù-ni-a-tí.,"To Uṣur-ša-Aššur from Ili-idi. I went up to the palace in accordance with your instruction, and I discussed your instructions, so the king said: ‘I will keep my word in accordance with what I have informed him’. The king also said: ‘I will write a letter to Wahšušana in regard to the gold and the fact that Šuluat brought a message, and then I will send a perdum-animal’. Urgent: do not go to Wahšušana. Until the rabi sikkitim has made the king of Purušhaddum, Ušinalam and the Wahšušanean swear an oath, he will not come. Here in the Land of Šarla, the Šabueans kept us from the road and they have seized us.","Barjamovic, Gojko - A Historical Geography of Ancient Anatolia in the Assyrian Colony Period. CNI 38, 2011.pdf",392
a-na A-šùr-e-mu-qí qí-bí-ma um-ma Ma-ṣí-ì-lí-ma 4 GÚ AN.NA ù it-ra-sú ku-nu-ki ša A-limki na-áš-a-kum,To Aššur-emuqi from Maṣi-ili. I am carrying 4 talents of tin and extras sealed in the City.,"Barjamovic, Gojko - A Historical Geography of Ancient Anatolia in the Assyrian Colony Period. CNI 38, 2011.pdf",106
lu-qú-ut-kà šál-ma-at e-ma-ru-kà šál-mu-ú mì-ma li-ba-kà la i-pá-ri-id,Your goods are well. Your donkeys are well. Do not worry about a thing.,"Barjamovic, Gojko - A Historical Geography of Ancient Anatolia in the Assyrian Colony Period. CNI 38, 2011.pdf",106
a-na-kam ma-lá ṣú-ha-ru e-ru-bu-ni a-na pá-ni-a a-na sá-ra-dim,Here [you should return] all the retainers who enter (Kaneš) to me to act as packers.,"Barjamovic, Gojko - A Historical Geography of Ancient Anatolia in the Assyrian Colony Period. CNI 38, 2011.pdf",106
a-na kà-ri-im Kà-ni-iš qí-bi-ma um-ma ší-ip-ru-ku-nu ù kà-ru-um Wa-ah-šu-ša-na-ma ṭup-pè-e wa-bar-tum ša Ú-lá-ma ù Ša-lá-tù-ar ú-šé-bi4-lu-nim-ma ni-iš-ta-me-ma ni-ik-nu-uk-ma na-áš-ú-ni-ku-nu-tí i-ša-am-ší ṭup-pè-e ni-iš-ta-me-ú 2 ší-ip-ri ha-ra-an Ú-lá-ma-ma 2 ší-ip-ri ha-ra-an Ša-lá-tù-ar-ma a-na Pu-ru-uš-ha-dim a-na a-wa-tim za-ku-im ni-iš-ta-pár.,"To the Kaneš Colony from your envoys and the Wahšušana Colony. We have heard the tablets that the Stations of Ulama and Šalatuwar sent to us, we have sealed them, and now they are bringing them to you. The day we heard the tablets, we sent two messengers by the Ulama route and two messengers by the Šalatuwar route to Purušhaddum to clear the order.","Barjamovic, Gojko - A Historical Geography of Ancient Anatolia in the Assyrian Colony Period. CNI 38, 2011.pdf",348
Puzur4-A-na a-na Wa-lá-ma lá ak-ta-áš-dam a-na Ša-lá-tí-wa-ar i-ta-lá-ak,"I did not catch up with Puzur-Anna in Ulama, and now he has gone to Šalatuwar","Barjamovic, Gojko - A Historical Geography of Ancient Anatolia in the Assyrian Colony Period. CNI 38, 2011.pdf",348
a-na Ša-lá-tí-wa-ar ha-ra-na-tum lá na-ṭù a-[tù]-ar-ma a-na Ú-la-ma e-li.,"The roads to Šalatuwar are not feasible, so I will turn around and go up to Ulama.","Barjamovic, Gojko - A Historical Geography of Ancient Anatolia in the Assyrian Colony Period. CNI 38, 2011.pdf",348
a-šu-mì A-lu-wa ša a-na ta-hi-tim a-na Pu-ru-uš-ha-dim ša-áp-ru sí-hi-tum i-na Pu-ru-uš-ha-dim ha-⌈ra-num⌉ lu a-na Ú-lá-ma lu a-na Ša-lá-tù-ar lu a-na Ša-ba-a a-šar e-ra-bi-im ú-lá i-ba-ší a-šu-mì ki-a-am A-lu-wa a-na ṣé-ri-kà ú-ta-e-ra-šu,"Concerning Aluwa, who was sent to Purušhaddum for to gather information: there is turmoil in Purušhaddum. There is no road to enter either Ulama or Šalatuwar or here to Šabaya. For that reason I have returned Aluwa to you.","Barjamovic, Gojko - A Historical Geography of Ancient Anatolia in the Assyrian Colony Period. CNI 38, 2011.pdf",348
ha-ra-ni a-na Wa-ah-šu-ša-na a-ta-lá-ak,I have left on a journey to Wahšušana,"Barjamovic, Gojko - A Historical Geography of Ancient Anatolia in the Assyrian Colony Period. CNI 38, 2011.pdf",348
šu-ma Ša-ba-na-tum DAM Ku-zi-zi-a a-na Wa-ah-šu-ša-[na] ta-ta-lá-ak,"If Šabanatum, wife of Kuziziya, has gone to Wahšušana","Barjamovic, Gojko - A Historical Geography of Ancient Anatolia in the Assyrian Colony Period. CNI 38, 2011.pdf",348
iš-tù Dur4-hu-mì-it URUDU a-na Pu-ru-uš-ha-dim is-ri-id-ma 1 ANŠE-šu URUDU a-dí Wa-ah-šu-ša-na is-ri-⌈id-ma⌉ i-na ma-ṣa-ra-tim ša ha-ra-an Ú-la-ma ú-šé-ṣí-šu-nu ù a-tù-ra-am.,"He packed the copper (to go) from Durhumit to Purušhaddum, and he packed his own donkey to (go) as far as Wahšušana, and then I led them (the remaining donkeys) out with the help of the guard-posts on the Ulama road and I returned.","Barjamovic, Gojko - A Historical Geography of Ancient Anatolia in the Assyrian Colony Period. CNI 38, 2011.pdf",348
i-na 10 na-ru-uq ú 2 DÚG ŠE-im ar-ša-tí ša Pì-lá-ah-Ištar e-zi-ba-ni ŠÀ.BA 6 DUG a-na […] 4 DUG a-na ⌈X⌉-i-ša-ma ú-šé-bi4-il5,Out of 10 sacks and 2 pots of barley that Pilah-Ištar left for me I brought 6 pots to […] and 4 pots to Taišama,"Barjamovic, Gojko - A Historical Geography of Ancient Anatolia in the Assyrian Colony Period. CNI 38, 2011.pdf",224
ša-ni-tam mAb-du-⌈e⌉[ra-ah] iš-tu Za-al-baki il-[li-kam-ma] LUGAL ša Ur-siki ik-ta-la-šu um-ma-a-mi GIŠ.MÁ.GEŠTIN.NA lu-ma-kum-ma a-li-ik [i-d]i-im lu-ud-di-na-ak-kum ù a-l[i-i]k a-na Kar-ka-mi-iski ⌈il-li-kam⌉-ma it!(da)-ti-ia in-na-me-er ù ut-[t]e-er-šu a-na Ur-si-imki-ma um-ma ⌈a-na-ku-ma⌉ a-li-ik hu-um-ṭà-am ù ⌈a⌉-[li-ik i-d]i-šu LÚ Za-al-baki i-na Ka[r-ka-mi-is]⌈ki⌉-ma wa-š[i-ib],"Second, Abdi-erah was coming here from Zalba, but the king of Uršu detained him, saying: ‘I will fill your wine-boat, and I will also provide you with an escort, and then (you can) leave’. He then came here to Carchemish and met with me, and I returned him to Uršu, saying: ‘Go quickly’. His escort, a man from Zalba, stays in Carchemish.","Barjamovic, Gojko - A Historical Geography of Ancient Anatolia in the Assyrian Colony Period. CNI 38, 2011.pdf",215
md30-ti-ri a-na né-eh-ra-ri-im a-na ṣe-ri-ia iš-pu-ra-am-ma a-na ṣe-ri-šu a-na Šu-ba-at-dUTUki qa-du-[u]m ṣa-bi-im ak-šu-d[am],"Sin-tiri wrote to me for help, so I went to him in Šubat-Šamaš together with the troops.","Barjamovic, Gojko - A Historical Geography of Ancient Anatolia in the Assyrian Colony Period. CNI 38, 2011.pdf",215
ša-né-em u4-um-[š]u ṭe4-mu-um ša na-ak-ri-im im-qú-ut [u]m-ma-mi Ia-pa-ha-dIM a-lam Za-al-lu-ulki i-na a-ah ÍDBURANUN e-bé-er-tam an-ni-tam i-pu-úš ù qa-du-um 2 li-im ṣa-bi-im ha-bi-ri ša ma-a-tim i-na li-ib-bi a-lim ša-a-ti wa-ši-ib,"The following day a letter with a message about the enemy came, saying: ‘Yapah-Adad has taken up position at the town of Zallul on the bank of the Euphrates on the opposite bank from here, and together with 2,000 men – hāpiru of the land – he is now staying in that town’.","Barjamovic, Gojko - A Historical Geography of Ancient Anatolia in the Assyrian Colony Period. CNI 38, 2011.pdf",215
a-wa-tum an-ni-tum im-qú-ta-an-ni-ma iš-tu Šu-ba-at-dUTUki qa-du-um ṣa-bi-im ša ma-ah-ri-ia ù qa-du-um ṣa-bi-im ša ma-ha-ar md30-ti-ri ú-ud-di-id-ma a-lam Hi-mu-uški a-na pa-an a-lim Za-al-lu-ulki e-pu-uš,"This was the news that reached me, so I hastened with the men under my command and the men under Sin-tiri from Šubat-Šamaš, and I took up position in front of the town of Zallul in Himuš.","Barjamovic, Gojko - A Historical Geography of Ancient Anatolia in the Assyrian Colony Period. CNI 38, 2011.pdf",215
bi-ri-it a-la-ni [ki]-la-li-in 30 A.ŠÀ,"Between the two towns is a distance of 1,800 m.","Barjamovic, Gojko - A Historical Geography of Ancient Anatolia in the Assyrian Colony Period. CNI 38, 2011.pdf",215
ki-ma a-lam Hi-mu-uški a-na pa-ni-šu e-pu-šu ù né-eh-ra-ar ma-a-tim i-mu-ru i-ša-tam i-ša-tam iš-ši-ma a-la-nu-ú ka-lu-šu-nu ša e-bé-er-tim ša ma-a-at Ur-si-imki im-hu-ru-šu,"And when I took up position in Himuš and he saw the help of the land, he gave a fire-signal so that all the towns on the far bank of the land of Uršu, came to him.","Barjamovic, Gojko - A Historical Geography of Ancient Anatolia in the Assyrian Colony Period. CNI 38, 2011.pdf",215
ṣa-bu-um na-bu-[rum] ša i-[n]a zu-mu-ur SIG4 né-en-mu-du ma-ad-ma uš-šum ṣa-[b]a-am la i-ši-ib-bi-ru a-na a-lim[ki] ú-ul a-sà-a[n-ni]-iq,"The nabru-men that are behind the wall, and who have united, are many, and so to avoid spreading out the men, I will not go to the city.","Barjamovic, Gojko - A Historical Geography of Ancient Anatolia in the Assyrian Colony Period. CNI 38, 2011.pdf",215
ṭup-pí a-ni-[e-em] iš-tu a-ah ÍDBURANUN a-na ṣe-er be-lí-ia ú-še-bi-lam,"I send this, my message, to my lord from the bank of the Euphrates.","Barjamovic, Gojko - A Historical Geography of Ancient Anatolia in the Assyrian Colony Period. CNI 38, 2011.pdf",215
ṣa-bu-um ù bu-qá-ru ša-al-mu,The men and the livestock are well.,"Barjamovic, Gojko - A Historical Geography of Ancient Anatolia in the Assyrian Colony Period. CNI 38, 2011.pdf",215
i-na dUTU-ši ru-ba-um wa-áš-ha-na-i-um i-na sí-kà-tí-im i-tù-ra-ni.,"The day the King of Wašhaniya returns from the sikkātum,","Barjamovic, Gojko - A Historical Geography of Ancient Anatolia in the Assyrian Colony Period. CNI 38, 2011.pdf",340
áš-pu-ra-ku-nu-tí um-ma a-na-ku-ma AN.NA-ki ša bi-lá-tim ag-ra-ma a-na Ni-na-ša-a li-ší-ú-nim a-ša-me-ma a-li-ki a-na Wa-áš-ha-ni-a lá ú-šu-ru šu-ma Wa-ah-šu-ša-na-i-im ù Kà-ni-ší-im ša ma-mì-tám ub-lu-ni-ni ṭup-pí ik-ta-áš-dam i-na sí-ki-im dí-na-ma li-ší-ú-nim.,"I wrote to you, saying: ‘Hire some porters (from Kaneš) to bring my tin to Nenašša’. I hear that they will not set travellers free to go to Wašhaniya. If my letter has reached you (concerning that) they have brought the Wahšušanean and the Kanišite an oath, then give (the tin) in a sikkum so that they can bring it.’","Barjamovic, Gojko - A Historical Geography of Ancient Anatolia in the Assyrian Colony Period. CNI 38, 2011.pdf",340
šu-ma a-dí-ni i-Kà-ni-iš wa-áš-ba-tí a-na Wa-áš-ha-ni-a et-qá-ma a-dí ma-tum i-nu-hu lá té-ra-ba-am.,"If you are still in Kaneš, then travel to Wašhaniya, but do not enter until the Land settles down.","Barjamovic, Gojko - A Historical Geography of Ancient Anatolia in the Assyrian Colony Period. CNI 38, 2011.pdf",340
