pè-er-dí ša ta-áš-pu-ra-ni i-pá-ni-a ú-šé-ra-am a-wa-tí ša DAM GAL sí-sé-e ma-lá tág-mu-ru té-er-ta-kà lí-lí-kam.,He set the perdum-animals that you wrote to me about free (for sale) before I came. Let a your message come to me about the agreement you made with the wife of the chief of the horses.,"Barjamovic, Gojko - A Historical Geography of Ancient Anatolia in the Assyrian Colony Period. CNI 38, 2011.pdf",373
i-nu-me a-na-ku ù A-ba-ba [a-ṣ]é-er Ì-lí-dan e-tí-qú-ni [i?-na? h]a-ra-nim lu a-dí u4-mì-i [a-nim n]i-is-hu-ru-ma a-wa-sú [x x] x-du-ku-ni ú iš-tù Ku-bu-ur-na-at a-dí Dur4-hu-mì-it ni-tù-ru-ni 1/2 MA.NA 4 GÍN KÙ.BABBAR ga-me-er.,"When Ababa and I travelled to Ili-dan we were delayed on the journey until this very day, so his case ... and we returned from Kuburnat to Durhumit – 34 shekels of silver was the expense.","Barjamovic, Gojko - A Historical Geography of Ancient Anatolia in the Assyrian Colony Period. CNI 38, 2011.pdf",273
a-na-ku a-na ṣé-er Ì-lí-dan a-na Ku-bu-ur-na-at e-tí-iq-ma wa-ar-ki-tí-ma Ma-ma-hi-ir a-ša-tám e-ta-ha-az a-na Dur4-hu-mì-it a-šu-mì-ki e-tí-iq-ma a-wa-tám ni-kà-ša-ad.,"I have personally travelled to Ili-dan in Kuburnat, and after I left, Man-mahir has married a wife. I shall go to Durhumit for your sake, and we shall settle the matter.","Barjamovic, Gojko - A Historical Geography of Ancient Anatolia in the Assyrian Colony Period. CNI 38, 2011.pdf",273
