[um-ma A-šùr]-re-ṣí [ù] A-šùr-tak-lá-ak-[ma] [a]-na Šu-Sú-en6 qí-bi4-ma,From Aššur-reṣi and Aššur-taklaku to Šu-Su’en:,"Barjamovic, Gojko - A Historical Geography of Ancient Anatolia in the Assyrian Colony Period. CNI 38, 2011.pdf",163
[šu]-ma Puzúr-A-šùr ha-ra-an [sú]-qí-nim-ma iš-tí [ṣ]ú-ha-ri-šu i-ṭá-ra-ad-kà [um]-ma a-ta-ma i-pá-ni-šu [l]e-tí-iq-ma [i-na] Hu-ra-ma ù-lá [Ku-š]a-ra KÙ.BABBAR [1 MA.NA iš]-tí DAM.GÀR-im [... l]á-al-qé [... ]-x-dí-šu-nu [... ]-x-i i-na [...] ú-lá i-na [Ku-š]a-ra ki-lá a-dí [x]-dí i-kà-šu-du-ni [u]m-ma a-ta-ma KÙ.BABBAR [i]š-tí DAM.GÀR-ri?-im?.,"If Puzur-Aššur wants to send you by the ‘Narrow Track’ together with his servants, you should tell him: ‘Let me go ahead of him, and let me take an interest-bearing loan of about [one mina] of silver with a merchant in Hurama or in [Kušš]ara [...] them [...] or hold it back in [Kušš]ara. Until [...] they catch up with you, you should say: ‘The silver is with the merchant’.","Barjamovic, Gojko - A Historical Geography of Ancient Anatolia in the Assyrian Colony Period. CNI 38, 2011.pdf",163
a-hi-i a-šu-<mì> a-mu-tí-kà [dí]-⌈ik⌉ KÙ.BABBAR ša šu-mì Lá-qé-ep [i]t-bu-lu KÙ.BABBAR [a]-mu-tim sú-re-e ša ta-dí-nu-šu-ni dí-ik a-li-ik-ma da-me-e ša a-hi-a šé-e.,My brother was killed because of your amūtum. The silver that he took away in the name of La-qep – surely he was killed for the silver for the iron that you gave to him. Go and sue for the blood-money for my brother.,"Barjamovic, Gojko - A Historical Geography of Ancient Anatolia in the Assyrian Colony Period. CNI 38, 2011.pdf",320
kà-ru-um dí-nam i-dí-in-ma a-dí da-mu ša DUMU Ša-lim-A-šùr i-kà-šu-du-ni e-ba-ar Ta-wi-ni-⌈a⌉ ma-ma-an ú-lá i-kà-ba-as ù a-na e-ri-iš-tí-šu lu i-na ra-bi-ú-tim lu i-na ṣa-hu-ru-tim ma-ma-an ú-lá i-za-az.,"The Colony passed a verdict that until they acquire the blood money for Šalim-Aššur’s son, no one may go via Tawiniya, and no one, either among the great men or among the small men, may carry out his wishes.","Barjamovic, Gojko - A Historical Geography of Ancient Anatolia in the Assyrian Colony Period. CNI 38, 2011.pdf",320
um-ma kà-ru-um-ma li-zi-iz i-na GÍR ša A-šùr li-it-ma ší-ma-am lá iš-ú-mu-ma a-na Ta-wi-ni-a lá ú-šé-bi-lu a-na e-ri-iš-tí Ta-wi-ni-a-i-im lá i-za-zu ú-lá ki-ma me-ra a-li-ku-nu a-na i-dim li-li-ik ú-lá né-nu a-pu-hi-šu GÍR ša A-šùr lu ni-it-ma,"Then the Colony said: ‘Let him step forward and swear upon the dagger of Aššur that he has neither bought nor sent any goods to Tawiniya, (and that) he will not carry out the wishes of the Tawiniyan. Alternatively, he can go to the River as (if he were) a citizen of your city, or we can swear upon the dagger of Aššur in his stead’.","Barjamovic, Gojko - A Historical Geography of Ancient Anatolia in the Assyrian Colony Period. CNI 38, 2011.pdf",320
um-ma ru-ba-um ù ru-ba-tum-ma ša ṭup-pá-am qá-at-ni ú-kà-lu ku-nu-tí ú-ta-ma-ku-nu a-wi-lam ru-a-nim šu-ma lá ta-ra-dí-a-ni-šu 1 MA.NA a-mu-tám ú-lá 10 MA.NA KÙ.GI dí-na-nim-ma a-hu-ku-nu lu-šé-er šu-ma lá ta-da-na lá ta-tù-ra-ma šu-um-šu lá ta-za-kà-ra a-hu-ku-nu me-et.,"The king and queen replied: ‘Since our hand holds the letter it is yourselves whom I will make swear your oath. Bring us that man. If you do not lead him here then give us one mina of amūtum or ten minas of gold so I may release your brother. If you do not pay up, then do not return and do not to mention his name again. Your brother will be dead’.","Barjamovic, Gojko - A Historical Geography of Ancient Anatolia in the Assyrian Colony Period. CNI 38, 2011.pdf",320
