a-šu-mì ša na-áš-pé-er-tí-kà áp-lá-ah-ma 36 TÚG ŠÀ.BA a-na A-ma-ri-im i-na Ša-lá-ah-šu-a e-zi-ma šu-ut-ma a-na kà-ší-im na-ru-qá-tim ša ku-nu-ki-a iš-tí ú-nu-tí-šu É kà-ší-im ip-qí-sú-nu 41 TÚG.HI.A-tí-kà a-na Hu-ra-ma ú-šé-tí-qám-ma ha-ra-an sú-qí-ni ar-de8-a-ma šál-ma-ku i-Ku-bu-ur-na-at wa-áš-ba-ku ni-is-ha-tim a-dan-ma a-ma-lá té-er-tí-kà lu-qú-ut-kà a-na Dur4-hu-mì-it a-ra-de8,"I was frightened by your message, so I left 36 of the textiles to Amarum in Šalahšuwa, and he entrusted the sacks sealed by me together with his own things to the kaššum-official (in) the kaššum-office. I made your (remaining) 41 textiles go to Hurama, I led them (onto) the Narrow Track, and now I (have arrived) safely. I am staying in Kuburnat. I will now pay the nishātu-tax, and in accordance with your message, I will lead your goods to Durhumit.","Barjamovic, Gojko - A Historical Geography of Ancient Anatolia in the Assyrian Colony Period. CNI 38, 2011.pdf",194
