ṭup-pu-a i-na Ha-qá i-ba-ší-ú a-ba-ú-a a-tù-nu KÙ.BABBAR ṣa-ru-pá-[am] li-iš-qú-lu-ma i-na ku-nu-ki-ku-nu ku-un-kà-ma šé-bi4-lá-nim šu-ma a-na Ha-qá a-li-ku-um DUMU um-mì-a-ni-im ša ki-sà-am i-ra-dí-ú lá-šu a-na Ší-ma-lá-ma a-na a-šar ša-lá-mì-im ep-ša.,"My tablets are in Haqa. Dear fathers, let them pay the silver, seal it with your seals, and have it sent here. If there is no affiliated trader in the possession of a ‘purse’ going to Haqa, then make it (travel) safely to Šimala instead.","Barjamovic, Gojko - A Historical Geography of Ancient Anatolia in the Assyrian Colony Period. CNI 38, 2011.pdf",129
3 GÚ [2]8 MA.NA a-wi-it Ì-lí-a-lim 10 MA.NA ša A-mur-A-šur 10 MA.NA ša I-dí-MAR.TU ŠU.NÍGIN 3 GÚ 48 MA.NA iš-tù A-limki a-dì A-pí-im 1 GÚ-tám 2 MA.NA 2 GÍN.TA ik-šu-dam 15 GÍN.TA qá-qá-da-tim 7 5/6 MA.NA 8 1/2 GÍN áš-qúl iš-tù A-[pí-im] a-dì ⌈Ha-qá⌉ 3 GÚ 40 [MA.NA] a-wi-sú 1 GÚ-tám 2 1/2 MA.NA 2 GÍN.TA ik-šu-dam 5 GÍN.TA qá-qá-da-tim 9 1/3 MA.NA 2 GÍN [áš]-qúl iš-tù Ha-qá a-dì Té-ga-ra-ma 3 GÚ 30 MA.NA a-wi-sú 1 GÚ-tám 1/2 MA.NA 4 GÍN.TA 1 5/6 MA.NA 9 GÍN áš-qúl 6 GÍN AN.NA ta-ší-a-tum i-ba-a-ba-at A-limki 5/6 MA.NA 5 GÍN i-na SA.TU ša Ha-qá 1/3 MA.NA 5 GÍN ša sà-e-tim 7 GÍN ša Pu-ra-tim 12 GÍN mu-ṭá-e.,"Three talents 28 minas (of tin) – the declared value of (the consignment belonging to) Ili-alum. Ten minas belonging to Amur-Aššur. Ten minas belonging to Iddin-Amurrum. In total three talents 48 minas. From the City to Apum 2 minas and 2 shekels per talent came on (as dātum-tax). Fifteen shekels was the head-tax. I paid 7 5/6 minas and 8 1/2 shekels. From Apum to Haqa its declared value was 3 talents and 40 minas. Two and a half minas and two shekels per talent came on (as dātum-tax). Five shekels each was the head-tax. I paid 9 1/3 minas and 2 shekels. From Haqa to Tegarama his shipment was three talents and 30 minas. At half a mina and 4 shekels per talent, I paid 1 5/6 mina and 6 shekels of tin. 6 shekels of tin was the transport cost for the outstanding claims in the City. 5/6 minas and 5 shekels in the mountains of Haqa. 1/3 mina and 5 shekels for sa’utum. 7 shekels for the Euphrates. 12 shekels were in deficit.","Barjamovic, Gojko - A Historical Geography of Ancient Anatolia in the Assyrian Colony Period. CNI 38, 2011.pdf",129
