abuki affumiki [ana] sériya ana aha[ziki] ifpuram u anaku suhariya u nafperti assér abiki assamiki ana sésu'iki aftapram apputtum ina famsi tuppi tafamme'ini amma[kam] ana abiki punu['ima] isti suhariya tib'ema atalkim wédaku mamman fa ina rêséya izzazzuma pasfaram isakkananni lassu summa isti suhariya la talliki ina Wahsusana mer'at Wahsusana ahhaz ih[dima atti] u suhariya la ta[sahhara] atalkanim,"Your father has written to me about you concerning (a proposal) to marry you; and I have then sent my servants and a missive to your father concerning you (with a proposal) to lead you out. Please, the very day you hear my letter, turn to your father there and then get up and leave together with my servants. I am alone/lonely. There is noone to stand by me or to lay my table. If you do not come together with my servants, I shall marry a girl from Wahsusana here. Take care, so that you and my servants are not delayed there. Come here!","Dercksen, J.G. et al. - Veenhof Anniversary Volume. PIHANS 89, 2001.pdf",145
