"ma-la KU.BABBAR, i-na qé-tl-kà : ma-aq-tù : le-qé-/a-ma, is-ti KU.BABBAR : al-kam-ma : e-té-me, a-bi-ni ù pu-û-ut É a-bi-ni, za-ki-ma : lu su-um-kà : sa-li-um, i-sé-er É a-bi-ni : la i-sa-lâ","Take all the silver that might fall into your hands and come with (this) silver; free the spirits of our ancestors and 'the front of the house' of our father, for it is for your renown! A malicious man must not act badly toward the house of our father.","Michel, Cecile ed. - Old Assyrian Studies in Memory of Paul Garelli. PIHANS 112, 2008.pdf",191
"[su-ma]-me-en6 A-sùr DINGIR-ki ù e-ta-me, [a-be]-ni da-mi-iq-me-en6","If only Ashur, your god and the spirits of our ancestors, would show kindness...","Michel, Cecile ed. - Old Assyrian Studies in Memory of Paul Garelli. PIHANS 112, 2008.pdf",195
"a-hi a-ta :TOC', a-na KU.BABBAR : ta-er-ma, [s]é bi4 lam ki-ma, DINGIR ù e-té-me, ta-ga-mi-lu-ma, la a-ha-li-qir, e pu-us","You are my brother, sell the textiles for silver, then seal the silver and send it to me. Act so as to propitiate the god and the spirits so that I am not ruined!","Michel, Cecile ed. - Old Assyrian Studies in Memory of Paul Garelli. PIHANS 112, 2008.pdf",195
