"a-na-kam sa-i-la-tim, ba-ri-a-tim ù e-té-me, nu-sa-al-ma, A-sùr us-ta-na-ad-kà, KU.BABBAR ta-ra-am, na pa-as-ta-kà, ta!(ZA)-ze-ar i-na, a lim é' A sùr ma-ga-ra-am, fi-la ta-le-e, a-pu-turn ki-ma tup pa-am, ta-às-me-z al-kam-ma, e-en A-sùr : a-mu-ur-ma, na pa-as-ta-kà e-té-er","Here (in Aggur), we consult the dream interpreters, the divineresses and the spirits; the god Assur does not cease to warn you: you love (too much) money and despise your life! Can you not please the god Assur in the City (of Aggur)? Please, as soon as you have read (this) letter, come, visit the god Assur and save your life!","Michel, Cecile ed. - Old Assyrian Studies in Memory of Paul Garelli. PIHANS 112, 2008.pdf",194
