"a-su-mi [KÙ].BABBAR, ik-ri-bi4 sa a-bi4-ni, Be-la-turn a-na-kam, ta-am-ra-as, ù i-na û-tù-ki, ù i-na e-ta-me, sa-am-th-a-ni a-ma-kam, a-na Pu-su-ke-en 6 pu-nu-a-ma, AN.NA ù TÙGb°-r' : a-ma-lé, i-le e ir : li-di-ma, KU.BABBAR li-ik-nu-uk-ma, lu sé bi 4 la ma na pa-érs-ta-ak-nu, ù na per ors ti ni, li-té-er a-na-kam, lam-ni-is : i-lu-um, É a-bi4-ku-nu : e pa-as","Because of the silver, the ikribu-offerings of our father, here Belatum is sick, and we are mistreated by the demons and by the spirits of the dead! There, turn to Pusu-ken so that he sells all the tin and all the textiles he can, seals the silver and sends it to save your lives and our lives! Here, the god is treating your father's house badly!","Michel, Cecile ed. - Old Assyrian Studies in Memory of Paul Garelli. PIHANS 112, 2008 (2).pdf",104
