"su-ma a-na Ha-hi-im ta-pa-la-ah, a-na Ur-su-ma a-li-ik, a pu-tum a pu-tum we di-kà-ma, a-li-ik is-ti ELLAT, a-na Ma-ma la té-ra-ab, ù ma-la té-er-ti, a-lim' ELLAT"" a-hi-kà, a-na sal-si-îu, li pè-er-sù-ma pà-ni-ù-um, i-Ma-ma lu-si-ma a-na, ma-at Kà-ni-iî, ik-ku-du sa-ni-um, i-na Ur-su lu-si, ù sa-li-iî-tum, ki-a-ma lu-si.","If you fear (to go) to Hahhum, (then) go instead to Ursu. I beg you, please, go there alone! You must not enter Mama with the caravan, and according to the instructions (of the authorities) of the City (of Assur), your brother's caravan must be divided into three: the first (convoy) must leave from Mama, and (when) it has reached the land of Kanis, the second (convoy) must leave from Ursu, and the third (convoy) must leave in the same way.","Michel_2008_RANT5_Des Paragrinations des Marchands Assyriennes. RANT 5, 2008 371-388.pdf",10
